  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Black Friday Sale is mapped onto the transatlantic slave trade scene",
  "description": "The text 'black friday sale' is juxtaposed with the visual scene of the transatlantic slave trade, creating an analogical mapping where the commercial event is equated with the historical commodification of human beings. This mapping uses the term 'black' to reference both the racial identity of the enslaved people and the color associated with the sale, thereby reducing the trauma of slavery to a commercial promotion. The mapping is hateful and racially charged, leveraging historical suffering to mock or trivialize the Black Friday shopping event.",
